            {
                "entry_id": "632d37dd-fd62-304a-947c-9c63634e1233",
                "word": "giaour",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "403ff6c8-18f8-4713-bd1a-82c0f2c3086b",
                        "entry_id": "632d37dd-fd62-304a-947c-9c63634e1233",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "giaours"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "8b981082-8418-4890-bde8-6f7ae5576d96",
                        "entry_id": "632d37dd-fd62-304a-947c-9c63634e1233",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "ghiaour"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4cdbf6ad-fec5-39ad-8799-c1015ef6c1e4",
                        "entry_id": "632d37dd-fd62-304a-947c-9c63634e1233",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Infidèle ; mécréant ; non-musulman."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "offensive",
                            "pejorative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e4c13c69-742d-49d6-a53e-09f0971262c9",
                                "sense_id": "4cdbf6ad-fec5-39ad-8799-c1015ef6c1e4",
                                "text": "Ce giaour, son Athènes natale abandonnée, vécut à Prague, à Florence, à Cologne, puis devint littérateur français à Paris."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "565af927-9b73-4423-b06c-d9e985adee5c",
                                "sense_id": "4cdbf6ad-fec5-39ad-8799-c1015ef6c1e4",
                                "text": "— Et n'est-ce pas la ruine du glorieux empire de Soliman et d'Amurath, que ce retard général de toutes nos institutions? Les giaours ont marché, et nous, nous voilà toujours stationnaires ! Aussi les giaours nous battent, nous refoulent. Vois : à Tchesmé, les Russes brûlent nos vaisseaux; à Aboukir, Bonaparte rejette dans la mer nos régiments; à Héliopolis, Kléber défait, avec dix mille des siens, soixante mille des nôtres ! Partout, partout des défaites, et si nous cherchons parmi les giaours le secret de leurs victoires, nous sommes des giaours, disent les imans. Non, par la barbe de Mahomet ! mous ne sommes pas des giaours."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a08077df-87c6-435c-adf5-bc97dbc84c65",
                                "sense_id": "4cdbf6ad-fec5-39ad-8799-c1015ef6c1e4",
                                "text": "Aziyadé me regardait fixement. Devant un Turc, elle se fût cachée ; mais un giaour n’est pas un homme."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b1871ef5-551a-4a4c-9481-0fed931fc0cf",
                                "sense_id": "4cdbf6ad-fec5-39ad-8799-c1015ef6c1e4",
                                "text": "Giaour. Expression farouche, d'une signification inconnue, mais on sait que ça a rapport à l'Orient."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fe0c63ba-fbae-4564-a284-be2688f02b56",
                        "source_entry_id": "632d37dd-fd62-304a-947c-9c63634e1233",
                        "source_sense_id": "4cdbf6ad-fec5-39ad-8799-c1015ef6c1e4",
                        "target_lang_word": "giaour",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "giaour",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e00d2797-2b2e-396f-b2bc-b24e2d1fdc80",
                                        "entry_id": "72290b04-6d8a-3ac7-ad02-78567257a715",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A non-Muslim, especially a Christian, an infidel; especially as used by Turkish people with particular reference to Christians such as Greeks, Armenians, Bulgarians, Serbs and Assyrians."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slur"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c766cf6-4dc4-47de-ae87-cb90f56a67ee",
                                                "sense_id": "e00d2797-2b2e-396f-b2bc-b24e2d1fdc80",
                                                "text": "And far beyond the Moslem's power / Had wrong'd him with the faithless Giaour."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f243fef-de98-4a65-8598-9d70a580cae4",
                                                "sense_id": "e00d2797-2b2e-396f-b2bc-b24e2d1fdc80",
                                                "text": "We men are not a race of freebooters or giaours; not when our argosies are prey and food to the evil fish-of-metal whose lair is a German U-boat."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71d0c561-2f05-4dd5-a51b-95bc0f86b755",
                                                "sense_id": "e00d2797-2b2e-396f-b2bc-b24e2d1fdc80",
                                                "text": "I shudder in delight when I think of two-hundred-year-old books, dating back to the time of Tamerlane, volumes for which acquisitive giaours gleefully relinquish gold pieces and which they carry all the way back to their own countries[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ecd4d5e4-5d48-43fe-8fa0-3015356e79e1",
                                                "sense_id": "e00d2797-2b2e-396f-b2bc-b24e2d1fdc80",
                                                "text": "Byron’s tale called The Giaour is supposed to be told by a Turkish fisherman who had been employed all the day in the gulf of Ægi’na, and landed his boat at night-fall on the Piræus, now called the harbor of Port Leonê.[…]The tale is this: Leilah, the beautiful concubine of the Caliph Hasson^([sic]), falls in love with a giaour, flees from the seraglio, is overtaken by an emir, put to death, and cast into the sea. The giaour cleaves Hassan’s skull, flees for his life, and becomes a monk."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "69891585-4ce3-4297-a128-74115c0bdb8f",
                        "source_entry_id": "632d37dd-fd62-304a-947c-9c63634e1233",
                        "source_sense_id": "4cdbf6ad-fec5-39ad-8799-c1015ef6c1e4",
